up-type="author"><name><surname>Sever</surname><given-names>S.</given-names></name><name><surname>Damke</surname><given-names>H.</given-names></name><name><surname>Schmid</surname><given-names>S.L.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Garrotes, springs, ratchets, and whipsputting dynamin models to the test</article-title><source>Traffic.</source><volume>In press</volume><year>2000</year></citation></ref><ref id="ShepardandYaffe1999"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Shepard</surname><given-names>K.</given-names></name><name><surname>Yaffe</surname><given-names>M.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The yeast dynamin-like protein, Mgm1p, functions on the mitochondrial outer membrane to mediate mitochondrial inheritance</article-title><source>J. Cell Biol.</source><volume>144</volume><year>1999</year><fpage>711</fpage><lpage>719</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10037792</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Smirnovaetal1998"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Smirnova</surname><given-names>E.</given-names></name><name><surname>Shurland</surname><given-names>D.</given-names></name><name><surname>Ryazantsev</surname><given-names>S.</given-names></name><name><surname>van der Bliek</surname><given-names>A.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A human dynamin-related protein controls the distribution of mitochondria</article-title><source>J. Cell Biol.</source><volume>143</volume><year>1998</year><fpage>351</fpage><lpage>358</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9786947</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="StevensandWhite1979"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Stevens</surname><given-names>B.J.</given-names></name><name><surname>White</surname><given-names>J.G.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Computer reconstruction of mitochondria from yeast</article-title><sou